{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>giving you all the days.</b> That is, because He said to them ״לְמַעַן תַּאֲרִיךְ יָמִים עַל הָאֲדָמָה״ — Moses was concerned lest they say that the intention is that by virtue of their deeds it is that HaShem lengthens their days upon the land, and from an inference one learns that HaShem limited the days of the giving of the land just as He limited the life of man, as it is written (Job 14:5) ״אִם חֲרוּצִים יָמָיו,״ and He promised them to lengthen their days when they walk in a straight path. Therefore He concluded and explained <b>אֲשֶׁר HaShem Eloheikha נוֹתֵן לְךָ כָּל הַיָּמִים</b> — meaning, for the gift of HaShem is for all eternity, not for a limited time. And from now on His saying <b>וּלְמַעַן תַּאֲרִיךְ יָמִים</b> means that they would not die upon it in shortness of years, in the manner of His saying (Deuteronomy 11:21) ״לְמַעַן יִרְבּוּ יְמֵיכֶם״ etc. And His saying <b>כָּל הַיָּמִים</b> is the establishment of the land in the hand of Israel."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:15:17.574780632Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}